@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

# Sync Carbon Inventory Lines - Batch create, update, and delete operations
# This endpoint allows atomic synchronization of multiple line changes in a single request
#
# A line states how its factor was chosen through `factorSelection`, a tagged
# union. The variants carry disjoint data, so catalog validation cannot be
# bypassed by dressing a custom factor up as a catalog one:
#
#   CATALOG    the canonical emission_factor row plus the unit to express it in.
#              Value, source and year are NOT sent — the server reads all three
#              from the row, so a request cannot persist a number the catalog
#              disagrees with.
#   CUSTOM     a factor the organization typed in itself.
#   DIRECT     a total in tons, declared with no factor at all.
#   UNCHANGED  update only: keep the snapshot the line already has. The server
#              copies it verbatim and never reads the catalog.
#
# `factorSelection: null` means the line is still incomplete.
# `inputType` is DIRECT for a declared total, SIMPLIFIED otherwise.

### Sync Lines - Create only (new empty lines)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carbon-inventories/1/lines/sync HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "create": [
    {
      "subcategoryId": "1",
      "inputType": "SIMPLIFIED",
      "dimensionValue1Id": null,
      "dimensionValue2Id": null,
      "measurementUnitId": null,
      "quantity": null,
      "factorSelection": null,
      "comment": null
    }
  ],
  "update": [],
  "delete": []
}


